WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.969
- I am not surprised to
see the end of Trump's,

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:88% position:13%
at least first four
years ending chaotically

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.241
since that is how they began,
and that is how they went.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that is why he was
elected in the first place,

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.778
to be a disruptor.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.881
So why are people so shocked
that he continues to disrupt?

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.450
(bright music)

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- All right, this is "The
Rubin Report," I'm Dave Rubin.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.427 line:0%
and we are doing a quick
on-the-fly interview today

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.362 line:0%
because I mentioned on
the show the other day,

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.031
I don't know who
to trust anymore.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.565
I don't know who's making sense.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.502
I don't know who's looking
at the world with clear eyes

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.504
and I went through
my mental rolodex

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.539
and Megyn Kelly popped up.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.643
And Megyn, you agreed to
do the show just like that.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.812
And here we are. How you doing?

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.181
- I'm doing well. For
you, Dave, anytime.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.750
Clear eyes, full
heart, can't lose.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.055
- All right, well, here are my
notes for today's interview.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.158 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh, (laughing) You're
just like Amy Coney Barrett.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.692
- I got nothing.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.528
Although my guys did tell me,
this is gonna air on Sunday.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.029
We're taping this
Friday afternoon.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.864 align:start size:81% position:19%
So people will
have to bear with,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:97% position:3%
if any little crazy vote got
changed or anything else.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:13.606
But generally speaking, as we
tape this on Friday afternoon,

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.510
how are you feeling about
the state of this election?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.081
The media portion of it,
the recount portion of it,

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.516
Biden, Trump, the
whole damn thing.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.687 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I have a lot of thoughts,
a lot of thoughts.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.456
- (laughing) Let's do
'em, one at a time.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.192 line:0%
- I am not surprised to
see the end of Trump's,

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
at least first four
years ending chaotically

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.464 line:0%
since that is how they began,
and that is how they went.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is why he was
elected in the first place

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.500
to be a disruptor.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.035
So why are people so shocked

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he continues to disrupt
right up to the last,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.107
what appear to be the
last final moments of,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.843
if not his presidency,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
the time in his presidency
before election?

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.081
I think Trump has lost. I do.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.016
I know people don't
want to hear that,

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.685
but I think he's lost.

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.386
And I think a lot of people

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.455
are struggling to
accept it, right?

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:06.559
It's like a grief process.
The first step is denial.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.465
We should do all the stuff.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.900
We should check out what's
happening in Pennsylvania.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
He should see those
legal challenges through.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.604
We should make sure we
have a Wisconsin recount,

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.405
and a Georgia recount.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.709
But my assessment from
where I sit out here

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
is there are not
enough gettable votes

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.714
even if he can prove fraud
or some untoward process

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.350
with the mail-in votes, to
get him over the top anymore,

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.118
that phase has passed.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.088
- Do you have faith
that the numbers

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.457
that we're getting are real?

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you have faith that not
only the people on the ground,

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.127
in whatever state
you want to pick,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:44.130
whatever city you want to
pick, are being honest,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.899
and that is being
translated to us

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:49.169
honestly through the media,
do you have faith in that?

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.504
- Not utter faith,
but enough faith.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.174
These are the same people who
did the count four years ago

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:57.877
and he won, so let's be real.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.513
They didn't just
become fraudulent,

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:84% position:16%
vote counters in
the past four years.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:05.618
And they also hated
him four years ago.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.153
It's not like they loved him.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.621
They thought he was going to
be full of love and rainbows

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.889
when he got into office.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.025
They wanted to kill
him four years ago.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.294
And you know, Philadelphia's
famous for its voter fraud.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:18.898
And so these problems have
existed long before now.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.334
And what I'm seeing in the
electoral process is, to me,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:24.637
it's akin to when we
went HD in television,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.739
where everything
looked just fine

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.241
when it was a little fuzzy.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then, when you could see
it up close and personal,

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.945
it was like, my eyes!

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.380
Oh, my God! I didn't want
to see this, it's hideous.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.016
And that's what's happening
with our electoral process.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.185 align:start size:84% position:16%
It isn't perfect,
it's far from perfect.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:41.321
It's the best we have.
Should we do better?

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.556
Can we do better? Yes.
And yes. Hello Florida.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:47.093
Let's just be like Florida,
but we're not right now.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:50.063
And we're not going to
get it to the point of,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.365
ah, now it's perfect.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we can perfectly know that
every vote that was proper

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
was counted and every
one that wasn't, was not.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.038
It's not going to
happen, people.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.974
That's not the way
our system is built.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:03.076
So we're gonna have
to do good enough.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.078
That's how the system's set up.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.447
Even the votes he's counting,
even the ones he was like,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
that was fraudulently filled
out, or that's ba ba ba,

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:12.552 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're talking about handfuls,
handfuls here and there.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:15.788
You're not talking
about 70,000 votes

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's gonna get him
over the top in Arizona,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.193
that's not going to happen.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
The places where it's
tightest, Biden is ahead.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
Biden is ahead right
now in Georgia.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:29.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
Biden is ahead in a
couple of these states

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.204
that Trump is contesting.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.941
So I just think the odds of
Trump turning this around

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.176
right now are infantesimal.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:40.513 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so I'm not saying
it's totally impossible,

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.749
but realistically, if you
want to know what I think,

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.818
I think he's lost and I don't
think his legal challenges

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.654
or the recounts are
gonna amount to much.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.922
- Yeah. So, what do
you think he'll do?

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you think he
just runs the table

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.694
with every legal
course of action

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
and just does
absolutely anything?

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.631
Or do you sense that
maybe at some point,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.932
if what you're saying is right,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.601
that he will throw in the towel?

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.836
- I know the throwing in the
towel doesn't sound like Trump.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.773 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I also think he owes
it to his supporters

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:10.943
who love him and don't trust
these systems for good reasons

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.445
to see these challenges through.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.247
I have no problem with
him stoking those fires

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start position:0%
and getting in there and making
sure, to the extent he can,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
maybe it's his final
act as president

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:22.622
right before his lame
duck period to disrupt

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.858
yet another system to
upend it, blow it up,

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.593
and ultimately make
it better, right?

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.462
Tear it down so we
can come back better

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.030
for the next four year period.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:35.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I support his
willingness to challenge,

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.038
where he has good faith
evidence of a problem,

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.406 align:start size:81% position:19%
like what happened
in Pennsylvania

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.475
with allowing the mail-in votes

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.043
to be postmarked
on election day,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:47.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
something that was approved
by judges and not legislators,

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.449
which is not okay.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.850
The court refused to
take that challenge.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.352
They said, get back to us

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.953
if this becomes an ongoing
problem after the election.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.288
And if there's a
split in the states

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.723
that we might have to resolve.

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.891
He should pursue
that, he should.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.494
But again, it doesn't look
like there are enough votes

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.730
in that pile that
could help him.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
Anyway, I think he
should see it through,

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.433
I don't think he should
give up before he has to,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.068
but I think realistically,

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it becomes
clear that he's lost,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.473 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're gonna need the people
who are closest to him,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:16.275
who he trusts, not the
media, which he doesn't,

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.978
for good reason, to
sit him down and say,

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:22.782
it's no longer about you,
this is about the country.

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:25.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
And there will be a
peaceful transfer of power.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.854
And while you can go
out there and say,

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:29.188 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have real problems
with the way

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.890
the system conducted itself.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.925
And I don't know
about this vote.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:36.929 align:start size:97% position:3%
I am going to pass the
torch and put America first

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.399
to quote somebody we all know.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:43.102
- Do you think that part
of his calculation of,

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.371 align:start size:84% position:16%
even if he sees
it, that he's lost,

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.839 align:start size:84% position:16%
like the challenges
aren't going anywhere?

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.208
That part of it will be
the burn it down thing,

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:52.412 align:start position:0%
because even just a few
minutes before we started here,

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:55.882
I saw a tweet by
AOC and, in effect,

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.817
we're going to have
to come for Trump,

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.820
they keep saying enablers and
the sycophants and whatever.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
And it's like, a few
weeks ago, Robert Reich,

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.458 align:start size:84% position:16%
who was in the
Clinton administration

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.260
talked about a truth and
reconciliation commission

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.629
and that these people love lists

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.297
and all of these weird things.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:14.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like, for all
the chants of lock her up,

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.401
it never happened.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was nobody knocking
on Hillary's door

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.838
that Trump may feel,

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:22.175 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think actually for good
reason that these people,

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:24.310 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether the guy did
anything illegal or not,

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.747
they've created this monster
in their heads, let's say,

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:30.817 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that they will do
things that are unimaginable

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the American
political landscape.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.855
- I think, yes, they will.

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.891
It's not paranoia when they
really are out to get you.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.160
And that explains a lot
of Trump's behavior.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.996
I think the media
is so disgusted

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
by his rhetoric from
the White House.

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:48.000 align:start position:0%
And they're like, it's not
great. I'm not gonna defend it.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.102 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I understand where
he's coming from.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:53.873 align:start size:97% position:3%
They have been out to get
him for more than four years.

00:07:53.873 --> 00:07:58.878 align:start size:97% position:3%
The media is his enemy. They
absolutely are his enemy.

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:04.050 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the Democrats loathe
him in a special way.

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:08.287
One does have to wonder if a
lot of these Democrats think

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:09.655
the ends justify the means.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:14.527
We really have had a baseless
attempt to impeach the guy

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:16.662
that was right on the heels

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:21.000
of a completely made up
Russia investigation,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.736
and not to mention all
the non controversies

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:26.272 align:start size:88% position:13%
the media fed off of
for the last four years.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:29.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
So he is right to
totally distrust them.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.210
The pollsters have
had it totally wrong

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.845
when it comes to
Trump all along.

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.780 align:start position:0%
I do want to make a distinction
between the pollsters

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.016
who predict vote
prior to the vote

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:39.252
and the people at
the decision desks

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:42.989 align:start size:88% position:13%
who analyze for a
living raw vote tallies,

00:08:42.989 --> 00:08:45.424
two totally different animals.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.792 align:start size:88% position:13%
So just because we don't
trust the pollsters

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.995
like Nate Silver doesn't
mean we shouldn't trust

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:51.230 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Fox News Decision
Desk, but anyway,

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump has a general
distrust of these systems,

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.434 line:0%
that's well-founded.

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.638 line:0%
And so do his fans.

00:08:58.638 --> 00:09:00.106 line:0%
And that's why I think people
aren't being nuts right now.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:02.208 line:0%
It's not crazy conspiratorial,

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:06.479
but it's based on data
it's based on experience.

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:09.649
And to expect the left
to understand any of that

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.417
is too much to expect.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:14.086
They won't. There isn't
grace on the other side.

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:16.389
I mean, there's great guys
like Andrew Yang, right?

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:18.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who's saying all the right
things, like be cool.

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:20.560 align:start size:84% position:16%
And let's not go too
far and whatever.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.529
And then there's just jerks
like AOC or Nancy Pelosi

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:25.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
coming out and saying,
we have a mandate,

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.832 align:start size:88% position:13%
which you don't even
have close to a mandate.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.234
and one other point on her,

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.669
the more you say
you have a mandate,

00:09:29.669 --> 00:09:31.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
which you clearly do
not, you lost House seats

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:33.072
instead of gaining
them, it looks like

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:34.607
you're not gonna have
control of the Senate,

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:38.010
you didn't get the Blue Wave
at the presidential level,

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.780
the more the Republicans, if
they do take over that Senate

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.617
are gonna do to stymie every
piece of Joe Biden's agenda.

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:47.420
There will be no grace
on their side either.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.822
- I actually read your
tweet about Nancy Pelosi

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:51.958
and the mandate on
my show this morning.

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:55.561
And I was trying to frame it
in a way that will give people,

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:57.863
obviously a lot of my
